965
00:39:02.220 --> 00:39:04.380
How do we get you that job in your retirement?
我们怎么才能让你退休后得到那份工作呢？

966
00:39:04.380 --> 00:39:07.520
I just opened—oh, that is a perfect retirement job.
我刚打开——噢，那真是份完美的退休工作。

967
00:39:07.740 --> 00:39:10.800
You have a stack of the presidential seal responses.
你有一叠总统印章的回复函。

968
00:39:11.120 --> 00:39:11.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

969
00:39:11.760 --> 00:39:13.760
You open people's wedding invites.
你拆开人们的婚礼请柬。

970
00:39:14.020 --> 00:39:16.860
I bet I could have a window, have my hummingbird feeder.
我敢说我能有个窗户，还能放个蜂鸟喂食器。

971
00:39:17.840 --> 00:39:18.280
Lady.
天呐。

972
00:39:18.400 --> 00:39:19.820
This is a perfect job for me.
这对我来说真是份完美的工作。

973
00:39:20.280 --> 00:39:20.720
Wow.
哇。

974
00:39:21.240 --> 00:39:24.440
Well, Erin is completely intimidated by this news.
艾琳被这个消息彻底吓到了。

975
00:39:24.740 --> 00:39:25.120
Yeah.
是啊。

976
00:39:25.300 --> 00:39:28.120
She's going to have to see the first lady at holidays now?
她以后过节得去见第一夫人了？

977
00:39:28.320 --> 00:39:28.540
Yeah.
是啊。

978
00:39:28.620 --> 00:39:30.140
What is she going to say at holiday dinners?
她在节日晚宴上该说什么呢？

979
00:39:30.140 --> 00:39:31.200
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

980
00:39:31.200 --> 00:39:32.000
The pressure.
压力好大。

981
00:39:32.600 --> 00:39:36.360
In the break room, Andy tells Clark and Pete that he's getting rid of all the junk food
在休息室里，安迪告诉克拉克和皮特他要清理掉所有的垃圾食品，

982
00:39:36.360 --> 00:39:39.620
because, in case they hadn't heard, he's now related to Michelle Obama.
因为如果他们还没听说的话，他现在和米歇尔·奥巴马是亲戚了。

983
00:39:39.800 --> 00:39:40.800
They applaud him.
他们为他鼓掌。

984
00:39:41.040 --> 00:39:41.320
Yes.
是的。

985
00:39:41.720 --> 00:39:43.660
Turns out they applaud him all the time.
结果他们一直在为他鼓掌。

986
00:39:43.840 --> 00:39:44.600
All the time.
一直都在。

987
00:39:44.980 --> 00:39:49.060
Well, Andy wants to remove this junk food partly because now he has this very strong connection
安迪想清理这些垃圾食品，部分原因是他现在和米歇尔·奥巴马的倡议有着非常紧密的联系，

988
00:39:49.060 --> 00:39:52.480
to one of Michelle Obama's initiatives that we need to get healthier.
我们需要变得更健康。

989
00:39:52.840 --> 00:39:53.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

990
00:39:53.520 --> 00:39:54.660
There was a scene.
当时有个场景。

991
00:39:55.740 --> 00:39:57.080
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

992
00:39:57.080 --> 00:39:59.140
And I had never heard this term before.
我以前从没听过这个词。

993
00:39:59.140 --> 00:40:01.840
And now I just want to use it for the rest of my life.
现在我余生都想用它。

994
00:40:03.240 --> 00:40:05.180
Andy flexes in front of everyone.
安迪在大家面前秀肌肉。

995
00:40:05.340 --> 00:40:08.060
You know, he comes out of his office and he does like the flex.
你知道，他从办公室出来，做了个秀肌肉的动作。

996
00:40:08.240 --> 00:40:08.500
Sure.
当然。

997
00:40:08.660 --> 00:40:09.980
Shows off his biceps.
展示他的二头肌。

998
00:40:10.680 --> 00:40:12.640
And then he shouts to the room.
然后他对着房间大喊。

999
00:40:12.800 --> 00:40:16.180
He says, I want someone to come slap my hang down.
他说，我想找人来拍打我的垂挂物。

1000
00:40:16.900 --> 00:40:17.660
What's that mean?
那是什么意思？

1001
00:40:17.880 --> 00:40:19.580
Jim says, what's a hang down?
吉姆问，什么是“下垂肉”？

1002
00:40:19.900 --> 00:40:23.120
And he said, it's the part that hangs down, you know, from your bicep.
他说，就是你肱二头肌下面垂下来的那部分，你知道的。

1003
00:40:23.200 --> 00:40:24.060
Your tricep?
肱三头肌？

1004
00:40:24.160 --> 00:40:24.440
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

1005
00:40:24.580 --> 00:40:24.960
Right here.
就在这儿。

1006
00:40:25.080 --> 00:40:25.280
Yep.
没错。

1007
00:40:25.280 --> 00:40:29.880
He's like, someone come slap my hang down because, you know, he's sort of like, it's
他说，谁来拍拍我的“下垂肉”，因为，你知道，他觉得那部分，

1008
00:40:29.880 --> 00:40:31.160
so rock hard, right?
硬得像石头一样，对吧？

1009
00:40:31.300 --> 00:40:31.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1010
00:40:31.620 --> 00:40:31.940
It's not going to hurt.
拍一下又不疼。

1011
00:40:32.400 --> 00:40:37.500
Meredith walks over and slaps the shit out of his hang down.
梅雷迪斯走过去，狠狠地拍了一下他的“下垂肉”。

1012
00:40:37.680 --> 00:40:38.800
And Andy's like, ow.
安迪就喊，哎哟。

1013
00:40:39.760 --> 00:40:43.360
But I mean, I had never heard that part of your body called the hang down.
但我是说，我从来没听过身体那个部位叫“下垂肉”。

1014
00:40:43.360 --> 00:40:44.700
I've got some hang down.
我也有点下垂肉。

1015
00:40:44.900 --> 00:40:46.280
I've got some hang down.
我也有点下垂肉。

1016
00:40:46.660 --> 00:40:47.420
You know what?
你知道吗？

1017
00:40:47.520 --> 00:40:52.060
I think to myself, thank goodness I'm not, you know, part of the royal family where I
我心想，谢天谢地我不是皇室成员，

1018
00:40:52.060 --> 00:40:55.900
have to put my arm up and wave because then you just see a jiggly hang down.
不用举起胳膊挥手，不然就会露出晃晃悠悠的下垂肉。

1019
00:40:56.340 --> 00:40:56.700
Oh.
噢。

1020
00:40:57.100 --> 00:40:57.800
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1021
00:40:57.920 --> 00:40:58.180
Yeah.
明白。

1022
00:40:58.580 --> 00:40:58.860
I had.
我有过。

1023
00:40:59.000 --> 00:40:59.580
Thank goodness.
谢天谢地。

1024
00:40:59.740 --> 00:41:03.460
That's the only reason I'm glad I'm not part of a royal family.
这是我庆幸自己不是皇室成员的唯一原因。

1025
00:41:04.080 --> 00:41:05.500
Everything else I could handle.
其他方面我都能应付。

1026
00:41:05.540 --> 00:41:06.440
You could do everything else.
其他方面你都能行。

1027
00:41:06.440 --> 00:41:07.840
I could do all the rest of it.
剩下的我都能应付。

1028
00:41:07.960 --> 00:41:11.520
But with my broken shoulder and my hang down, I'd have a hard time waving.
但因为我的肩膀受过伤，还有我的下垂肉，挥手对我来说太难了。

1029
00:41:11.760 --> 00:41:13.140
Otherwise, you would be in.
不然的话，你就能入选了。

1030
00:41:13.140 --> 00:41:14.280
Count you in.
算你一个。

1031
00:41:15.060 --> 00:41:19.200
One of my mom's sisters years ago, my aunt, I'll never forget.
我妈的一个姐妹，我姨妈，多年前的事，我永远忘不了。

1032
00:41:19.400 --> 00:41:24.240
She had reached a certain age and it was so hot out and she had a long sleeve on.
她到了某个年纪，那天特别热，她还穿着长袖。

1033
00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:25.740
And I was like, what are you doing in long sleeve?
我就问，你穿长袖干嘛？

1034
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:27.920
She's like, I haven't worn short sleeves in years.
她说，我好多年没穿过短袖了。

1035
00:41:28.200 --> 00:41:28.840
I was like.
我当时就……

1036
00:41:28.940 --> 00:41:29.780
Because of the hang down?
是因为下垂肉吗？

1037
00:41:30.060 --> 00:41:30.700
Because of the hang down.
是因为下垂肉。

1038
00:41:30.940 --> 00:41:32.560
Here's what I'm going to tell everybody.
我要告诉大家一件事。

1039
00:41:32.780 --> 00:41:33.720
Let it hang down.
让它垂着吧。

1040
00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:35.320
Hang it down.
让它垂下来。

1041
00:41:35.680 --> 00:41:36.980
Let it flap.
让它晃荡吧。

1042
00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:38.380
Hang it down now.
现在就让它垂着吧。

1043
00:41:38.600 --> 00:41:40.520
Life is too short.
人生苦短。

1044
00:41:40.520 --> 00:41:45.180
Is this the 50s that we were talking about a few episodes ago, Angela?
安吉拉，这就是我们几集前讨论的五十岁吗？

1045
00:41:45.480 --> 00:41:45.720
Yes.
是的。

1046
00:41:45.920 --> 00:41:53.980
Like my just like body, face, wrinkly neck, hang down body is just like, I'm just like,
就像我的身体、脸、皱皱的脖子、下垂的肉，我就是觉得，我挺好的。

1047
00:41:54.140 --> 00:41:55.280
I'm fine.
我很好。

1048
00:41:55.720 --> 00:41:56.800
Bring it on.
放马过来吧。

1049
00:41:57.080 --> 00:41:57.660
I'm fine.
我很好。

1050
00:41:57.800 --> 00:41:59.540
Worried about it in my 40s.
我在四十岁的时候还为此担心过呢。

1051
00:41:59.660 --> 00:42:01.960
In my 50s, I'm like, just whatever.
五十多岁了，我感觉就是，随它去吧。

1052
00:42:01.960 --> 00:42:06.480
You know, I have to tell y'all out there who are a lot younger than us, when you get to
你们知道吗，我得告诉那些比我们年轻得多的人，当你到了

1053
00:42:06.480 --> 00:42:11.420
your 50s, it's a real like liberating zero Fs chapter.
五十多岁，那真是一个完全不在乎别人怎么看的解放阶段。

1054
00:42:11.740 --> 00:42:12.000
Yeah.
没错。

1055
00:42:12.160 --> 00:42:14.400
We should all have started this in our 20s.
我们本该在二十多岁时就开启这个阶段的。

1056
00:42:14.820 --> 00:42:17.920
Maybe the next generation will have some of it.
也许下一代能领悟到一点吧。

1057
00:42:17.920 --> 00:42:18.560
Yeah, they'll figure it out.
是啊，他们会想明白的。

1058
00:42:18.760 --> 00:42:18.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1059
00:42:19.420 --> 00:42:24.280
Jim is now in Daryl's office and he's learning about batching and he's really into it.
吉姆现在在达里尔的办公室，他在学习批量处理，而且他对此非常着迷。

1060
00:42:24.440 --> 00:42:27.020
Andy comes in and Jim's like, you got to see this.
安迪进来了，吉姆说，你一定要看看这个。

1061
00:42:27.160 --> 00:42:28.080
This is really cool.
这真的很酷。

1062
00:42:28.080 --> 00:42:33.600
And Andy's like, I'm going to need you to be canned tuna right now.
安迪却说，我现在需要你闭嘴，金枪鱼罐头。

1063
00:42:33.980 --> 00:42:35.400
I don't want to hear from you.
我不想听你说话。

1064
00:42:35.500 --> 00:42:35.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1065
00:42:35.720 --> 00:42:36.640
Big tuna, zip it.
大金枪鱼，闭嘴。

1066
00:42:36.960 --> 00:42:39.460
That's when Andy tells Daryl his good news.
就在那时，安迪告诉了达里尔他的好消息。

1067
00:42:39.860 --> 00:42:40.920
Daryl is skeptical.
达里尔对此表示怀疑。

1068
00:42:41.580 --> 00:42:42.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1069
00:42:42.160 --> 00:42:43.000
But he's like, that's cool.
但他还是说，那挺酷的。

1070
00:42:43.420 --> 00:42:44.740
I have a fun fact.
我有个冷知识。

1071
00:42:44.900 --> 00:42:45.120
Okay.
好的。

1072
00:42:46.100 --> 00:42:49.660
Michelle Obama's brother is named Craig Robinson.
米歇尔·奥巴马的哥哥叫克雷格·罗宾逊。

1073
00:42:50.460 --> 00:42:51.420
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

1074
00:42:51.440 --> 00:42:52.380
How about that?
怎么样？

1075
00:42:52.400 --> 00:42:53.520
That's a crossover.
这真是个跨界联动。

1076
00:42:53.860 --> 00:42:54.820
It sure is.
确实是。

1077
00:42:54.820 --> 00:43:00.780
I also wanted everyone, when you're re-watching this episode and you see this scene, to please
我还想请大家在重温这一集看到这个场景时，

1078
00:43:00.780 --> 00:43:03.680
note that there's a lot of background action in this scene.
注意一下背景里有很多走动。

1079
00:43:04.240 --> 00:43:05.920
Creed does a cross to reception.
克里德走到了前台。

1080
00:43:06.220 --> 00:43:07.580
Meredith is at the copier.
梅雷迪思在复印机旁。

1081
00:43:07.940 --> 00:43:12.820
The reason for this is because Rain and I could not be at our desks in the background.
之所以这样，是因为雷恩和我当时不能坐在背景里的办公桌前。

1082
00:43:13.140 --> 00:43:17.220
And if we didn't have all that crossing, it would have just looked like an empty office.
如果我们没有安排那些走动，办公室看起来就会空荡荡的。

1083
00:43:17.640 --> 00:43:21.620
But, you know, Pam is supposed to be teaching Nellie to drive.
但你知道，帕姆本该在教内莉开车。

1084
00:43:21.620 --> 00:43:24.300
Dwight is supposed to be teaching Aaron Dothrocky.
德怀特本该在教亚伦·多斯罗基。

1085
00:43:24.580 --> 00:43:29.040
So this is something that they would do to prevent empty backgrounds.
所以这是他们为了避免背景空旷而采取的做法。

1086
00:43:29.740 --> 00:43:32.420
And I thought this scene was a good example of it.
我觉得这个场景是一个很好的例子。

1087
00:43:32.520 --> 00:43:33.140
I like it.
我喜欢。

1088
00:43:33.200 --> 00:43:33.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1089
00:43:33.900 --> 00:43:38.480
Well, let's go to break because when we're back, Nellie is eating a salad while driving.
好了，我们去休息一下，回来后，内莉要边开车边吃沙拉了。

1090
00:43:38.680 --> 00:43:38.840
Yes.
是的。

1091
00:43:38.860 --> 00:43:41.960
And I have a list for you.
我还有个清单要给你。

1092
00:43:42.260 --> 00:43:44.120
Best foods to eat while driving.
最适合开车时吃的食物。

1093
00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:45.260
Wait for it.
敬请期待。

1094
00:43:45.380 --> 00:43:48.280
I can't wait for it, but I will wait for it.
我等不及了，但我会等着看的。

1095
00:43:48.420 --> 00:43:49.160
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1096
00:44:00.300 --> 00:44:01.240
We're back.
我们回来了。

1097
00:44:01.240 --> 00:44:03.160
Pam is in the passenger seat.
帕姆坐在副驾驶座上。

1098
00:44:03.360 --> 00:44:04.280
Nellie is driving.
内莉在开车。

1099
00:44:04.720 --> 00:44:10.900
And on the console between the two of them is an open takeout container with a salad.
在她们两人之间的中控台上，放着一个打开的外卖盒，里面装着沙拉。

1100
00:44:11.520 --> 00:44:12.900
I don't know what kind of salad.
我不知道是什么沙拉。

1101
00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:13.520
Caesar salad.
凯撒沙拉。

1102
00:44:13.600 --> 00:44:14.540
There's big croutons.
面包丁很大。

1103
00:44:15.940 --> 00:44:18.220
Like, how is she eating the salad and driving?
话说，她是怎么做到一边开车一边吃沙拉的？

1104
00:44:18.540 --> 00:44:19.300
You know what?
你知道吗？

1105
00:44:19.300 --> 00:44:23.480
It was scripted that she would be eating a salad specifically.
剧本里写的就是她要吃沙拉。

1106
00:44:23.800 --> 00:44:24.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1107
00:44:24.720 --> 00:44:26.820
It was scripted that it was in her lap.
剧本里写的是放在她腿上。

1108
00:44:26.980 --> 00:44:27.680
It was, yes.
没错，确实是。

1109
00:44:27.680 --> 00:44:28.740
Well, here's the thing.
是这样的。

1110
00:44:28.860 --> 00:44:34.800
When we first did this scene, we did a take of Catherine holding the salad, like, kind
我们第一次拍这场戏时，拍了凯瑟琳拿着沙拉的一个镜头，大概是

1111
00:44:34.800 --> 00:44:39.020
of in her lap slash you couldn't see it when it was on her lap.
放在她腿上，或者说放在腿上时根本看不见。

1112
00:44:39.020 --> 00:44:40.680
So then she was kind of holding it up.
所以她当时是把它举起来的。

1113
00:44:41.020 --> 00:44:45.500
So we had some, like, visual issues because, you know, we had those little lipstick cams
我们遇到了一些视觉上的问题，因为你知道，我们用的是那种小型唇部摄像机，

1114
00:44:45.500 --> 00:44:47.560
and, you know, they only show so much.
你知道的，它们能拍到的范围有限。

1115
00:44:47.840 --> 00:44:51.720
So it's like, where can we put the salad where it's clear that she's eating a salad?
所以就在想，把沙拉放在哪里才能让人清楚地看出她在吃沙拉呢？

1116
00:44:51.720 --> 00:44:56.280
Yes, and we started with her kind of, like, holding it with one hand and having to take
是的，我们一开始让她用一只手拿着，不得不把手从方向盘上移开去吃。

1117
00:44:56.280 --> 00:44:58.380
her hand off the wheel to eat it.
那真的太搞笑了。

1118
00:44:58.560 --> 00:45:00.260
And it was so funny.
她真是一位了不起的肢体喜剧演员。

1119
00:45:00.740 --> 00:45:03.820
She is such an amazing physical comedian.
我知道这段素材肯定还在某处。

1120
00:45:04.300 --> 00:45:06.140
I know this footage is somewhere.
我当时笑得停不下来。

1121
00:45:06.460 --> 00:45:07.980
I couldn't stop laughing.
最终，我们觉得那样可能有点太不真实了。

1122
00:45:08.220 --> 00:45:12.080
Ultimately, we decided that it might be, like, a little too unrealistic.
我是说，那真的太搞笑了。

1123
00:45:12.620 --> 00:45:14.800
I mean, it was so funny.
顺便说一下，她在这些场景里其实并没有在开车。

1124
00:45:15.080 --> 00:45:17.780
And, you know, by the way, she's not actually driving in these scenes.
我们当时连接着一辆拖车，因为我的记忆里凯瑟琳

1125
00:45:17.780 --> 00:45:23.860
We're hooked up to, like, an insert car that's pulling us because my memory is that Catherine
不太会开车。

1126
00:45:23.860 --> 00:45:25.460
did not drive much.
她确实不会。

1127
