00:56:55.850 --> 00:56:56.190
Yes.
是的。

1486
00:56:56.190 --> 00:56:58.410
And now they're going to take it to the bullpen.
现在他们要把它带到办公区去展示了。

1487
00:56:58.590 --> 00:56:58.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1488
00:56:59.030 --> 00:57:00.750
Walking around, pointing to things.
四处走动，指指点点。

1489
00:57:00.950 --> 00:57:02.610
Does Aaron know what it is?
亚伦知道那是什么吗？

1490
00:57:03.050 --> 00:57:08.330
You know, Rain did a couple of interviews where he said that he absolutely loved doing this storyline.
你知道，雷恩做了几次采访，他说他非常喜欢拍这条故事线。

1491
00:57:08.630 --> 00:57:08.950
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1492
00:57:08.950 --> 00:57:12.030
And I guess there were even more scenes that got cut.
我想还有更多被剪掉的戏份。

1493
00:57:12.310 --> 00:57:18.610
He said he was most upset that there was a talking head where he is shirtless and he's speaking Dothraki.
他说他最难过的是有一段采访镜头被剪了，他在镜头里赤裸上身说着多斯拉克语。

1494
00:57:18.770 --> 00:57:18.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1495
00:57:18.970 --> 00:57:19.590
And it was cut.
结果被剪掉了。

1496
00:57:19.750 --> 00:57:20.610
He was very disappointed.
他非常失望。

1497
00:57:21.110 --> 00:57:21.450
Yes.
是的。

1498
00:57:21.630 --> 00:57:23.530
They're in the deleted scenes.
它们在删减片段里。

1499
00:57:23.830 --> 00:57:27.530
I didn't include them in my sharing today because it's a sight gag.
我今天分享的时候没把它们放进去，因为那是视觉笑话。

1500
00:57:27.750 --> 00:57:29.950
So, one, you can't see.
所以，首先，你看不见。

1501
00:57:30.130 --> 00:57:33.070
Angela, you are learning that we're on a podcaSt.
安吉拉，你得明白我们是在录播客。

1502
00:57:33.070 --> 00:57:33.530
I know.
我知道。

1503
00:57:33.850 --> 00:57:34.210
Listen.
听着。

1504
00:57:34.430 --> 00:57:34.710
It's wonderful.
这太棒了。

1505
00:57:35.010 --> 00:57:35.950
It's not going to last long.
但这持续不了多久。

1506
00:57:37.090 --> 00:57:39.310
But he's shirtless with no explanation.
但他没穿上衣，还没个解释。

1507
00:57:39.750 --> 00:57:45.170
And then he's got a talking head in Dothraki, which there are subtitles that you can't read.
然后他还有一段多斯拉克语的访谈，但字幕你根本看不懂。

1508
00:57:45.650 --> 00:57:48.430
I would say I think Rain did a very good job.
我觉得Rain做得非常好。

1509
00:57:48.690 --> 00:57:50.810
This is probably why he's sad it didn't make sense.
这大概就是他难过的原因，因为这根本说不通。

1510
00:57:50.810 --> 00:57:50.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1511
00:57:51.190 --> 00:57:53.570
Because he learned a whole talking head in Dothraki.
因为他学了整整一段多斯拉克语的访谈。

1512
00:57:53.910 --> 00:57:56.830
But, yeah, if you guys want to check him out, they're on the DVDs.
不过，如果你们想去看看他的表现，DVD里都有。

1513
00:57:57.150 --> 00:58:03.090
Well, as they move through the office speaking Dothraki, Pete says hi and Aaron responds in Dothraki.
嗯，当他们一边说着多斯拉克语一边穿过办公室时，皮特打了声招呼，而亚伦用多斯拉克语回应了他。

1514
00:58:03.310 --> 00:58:03.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1515
00:58:03.530 --> 00:58:04.930
And he's kind of like, I'm sorry.
他当时大概是那种，抱歉，我不懂。

1516
00:58:04.930 --> 00:58:06.610
Like, he's not really sure what's happening.
就像是，他不太确定发生了什么。

1517
00:58:06.910 --> 00:58:09.310
She also tries to speak Dothraki to Andy.
她还试着对安迪说多斯拉克语。

1518
00:58:09.570 --> 00:58:10.010
Yes.
是的。

1519
00:58:10.390 --> 00:58:13.090
He's asking if anyone's turned in their progress reports.
他问有没有人交进度报告。

1520
00:58:13.290 --> 00:58:15.050
And then he's like, what are you doing?
然后他就问，你在干什么？

1521
00:58:15.530 --> 00:58:18.890
Why would you learn a made-up language from a television show?
你为什么要学一门电视剧里的虚构语言？

1522
00:58:19.090 --> 00:58:22.150
And then she's like, Dwight, why didn't you tell me this was made up?
然后她就说，德怀特，你为什么不告诉我这是虚构的？

1523
00:58:22.190 --> 00:58:26.250
And he says, listen, people laughed at Klingon at first and now you can major in it.
他说，听着，人们起初也嘲笑克林贡语，但现在你都可以把它当专业来学了。

1524
00:58:27.190 --> 00:58:28.210
I had to know.
我必须得知道。

1525
00:58:28.470 --> 00:58:29.030
Can you?
真的可以吗？

1526
00:58:34.930 --> 00:58:40.310
You can study Klingon and Dothraki in college as part of linguistics courses.
你可以在大学里选修克林贡语和多斯拉克语，作为语言学课程的一部分。

1527
00:58:40.730 --> 00:58:46.490
In fact, I found out that Klingon is the most widely spoken fictional language.
事实上，我发现克林贡语是目前使用人数最多的虚构语言。

1528
00:58:46.490 --> 00:58:48.390
I do not doubt that.
对此我深信不疑。

1529
00:58:48.670 --> 00:58:51.250
That fandom is deep and strong.
那个粉丝群体的根基非常深厚。

1530
00:58:51.510 --> 00:58:55.870
The University of Texas at Austin offers a course where you study Klingon.
德克萨斯大学奥斯汀分校就提供克林贡语课程。

1531
00:58:56.030 --> 00:59:03.790
The University of Alaska Fairbanks has a course called Elfish, Klingon, and Dothraki Course in Development.
阿拉斯加大学费尔班克斯分校有一门课程，名字就叫“精灵语、克林贡语和多斯拉克语课程开发”。

1532
00:59:04.310 --> 00:59:05.850
Our son Jack learned Elfish.
我儿子杰克就学过精灵语。

1533
00:59:06.190 --> 00:59:07.850
What is Elfish for?
精灵语是干什么用的？

1534
00:59:08.010 --> 00:59:08.950
Is that Lord of the Rings?
是《指环王》里的吗？

1535
00:59:09.030 --> 00:59:09.330
Yes.
是的。

1536
00:59:09.990 --> 00:59:10.410
Oh.
噢。

1537
00:59:11.050 --> 00:59:15.630
So this is a whole thing, and I read about it, and now I didn't write down the name of it.
所以这已经形成了一种风潮，我读过相关资料，但现在我没记下它的名字。

1538
00:59:15.790 --> 00:59:27.270
But this idea of creating language, the creation of language, when you study these fictional languages, it's part of just understanding the creation of language in general.
但这种创造语言的理念，即语言的创造，当你研究这些虚构语言时，它其实也是理解语言创造整体过程的一部分。

1539
00:59:27.490 --> 00:59:32.690
This is what David talks about in the Wired magazine interview that I'm going to put in stories.
这就是大卫在《连线》杂志采访中提到的内容，我会把它放到故事里。

1540
00:59:32.690 --> 00:59:38.270
Well, I was also fascinated to find out that there is something called the Klingon Language Institute.
嗯，我还很惊讶地发现有一个叫“克林贡语言研究所”的机构。

1541
00:59:38.670 --> 00:59:47.510
It was founded in 1992 with, quote, the mission of bringing together individuals interested in the study of Klingon linguistics and culture.
它成立于1992年，引用其宗旨，是为了“将对克林贡语言学和文化感兴趣的人们聚集在一起”。

1542
00:59:47.510 --> 00:59:58.290
And as a side note, while reviewing, like, interesting college courses that are available, there is a course at Columbia College, Chicago,
顺便提一下，在浏览一些有趣的大学课程时，我发现芝加哥哥伦比亚学院有一门课，

1543
00:59:58.670 --> 01:00:02.690
and the University of Baltimore called Zombies in Popular Media.
还有巴尔的摩大学也有一门课，叫“流行媒体中的僵尸”。

1544
01:00:03.130 --> 01:00:04.510
You would like that.
你会喜欢这个的。

1545
01:00:04.870 --> 01:00:05.610
Sign me up.
算我一个。

1546
01:00:05.790 --> 01:00:06.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1547
01:00:06.810 --> 01:00:09.410
Fascinated by zombie culture, personally.
我个人对僵尸文化很着迷。

1548
01:00:09.810 --> 01:00:11.110
What is the culture?
僵尸有什么文化？

1549
01:00:11.290 --> 01:00:12.230
There is no culture.
根本没有文化。

1550
01:00:12.470 --> 01:00:13.330
They eat people.
他们只会吃人。

1551
01:00:13.530 --> 01:00:15.050
They moan about.
他们在那抱怨。

1552
01:00:15.050 --> 01:00:16.990
So they find another person.
所以他们又去找了别人。

1553
01:00:17.570 --> 01:00:24.130
There are so many things and debates about what zombies can do and not do and different iterations.
关于丧尸能做什么、不能做什么，以及各种不同的版本，有很多争论和说法。

1554
01:00:24.630 --> 01:00:35.830
Don't get me started on what happened when they remade the Dawn of the Dead movies and the zombies started moving fast because in the past, zombies only moved slow.
别跟我提翻拍《活死人黎明》时发生的事，那些丧尸开始跑得飞快，因为过去丧尸只会慢吞吞地走。

1555
01:00:36.050 --> 01:00:36.100
They were sluggish.
它们行动迟缓。

1556
01:00:36.570 --> 01:00:36.770
They lumber.
它们步履蹒跚。

1557
01:00:37.190 --> 01:00:37.330
Yeah.
没错。

1558
01:00:37.330 --> 01:00:43.870
Like, that's one of the things about them that is so scary is that, like, they can't run fast at you, but they never stop.
那种东西最可怕的一点在于，它们虽然跑不快，但它们从不停下。

1559
01:00:44.130 --> 01:00:46.690
Like, they will slowly gain ground.
它们会慢慢地逼近你。

1560
01:00:46.930 --> 01:00:49.050
And then they kind of back you into a corner.
然后把你逼进死角。

1561
01:00:49.750 --> 01:00:50.610
You know what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

1562
01:00:51.190 --> 01:00:51.690
Mm-mm.
嗯。

1563
01:00:51.850 --> 01:00:52.470
I don't.
我不明白。

1564
01:00:52.510 --> 01:00:54.010
That's what's scary about them.
这就是它们可怕的地方。

1565
01:00:54.110 --> 01:00:54.470
Mm-mm.
嗯。

1566
01:00:54.470 --> 01:00:57.230
But then all of a sudden, in the new movies...
但突然间，在那些新电影里……

1567
01:00:57.230 --> 01:00:58.110
They're speedy.
它们变得很快。

1568
01:00:58.250 --> 01:00:59.130
...fast moving.
……动作敏捷。

1569
01:00:59.450 --> 01:00:59.830
Mm-mm.
嗯。

1570
01:00:59.830 --> 01:01:00.490
Real quick.
非常快。

1571
01:01:00.910 --> 01:01:01.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1572
01:01:02.270 --> 01:01:02.750
Scariness.
太吓人了。

1573
01:01:03.390 --> 01:01:08.030
I'm sure there were Reddit threads abuzz about the fast versus slow moving zombies.
我敢肯定 Reddit 上一定有很多关于丧尸是该快还是该慢的讨论帖。

1574
01:01:08.570 --> 01:01:09.770
The zombie Reddit threads.
那些丧尸主题的 Reddit 帖子。

1575
01:01:10.010 --> 01:01:12.990
And I would think that that would be part of this college course.
我觉得那应该会是这门大学课程的一部分。

1576
01:01:13.430 --> 01:01:14.430
Jenna, you should take it.
珍娜，你应该去修这门课。

1577
01:01:14.610 --> 01:01:16.270
I wonder if there's an online version.
我在想有没有网课版本。

1578
01:01:16.470 --> 01:01:17.110
I am serious.
我是认真的。

1579
01:01:17.110 --> 01:01:18.050
You should take it.
你应该去修。

1580
01:01:18.270 --> 01:01:20.090
Would you take a Dothraki one?
你会去修多斯拉克语课吗？

1581
01:01:20.670 --> 01:01:22.610
Like, to learn to speak Dothraki?
就是，去学怎么说多斯拉克语？

1582
01:01:22.610 --> 01:01:23.430
I don't know.
我不知道。

1583
01:01:24.030 --> 01:01:26.470
I mean, it'd be a good party trick, I guess.
我是说，那应该是个不错的聚会表演节目吧。

1584
01:01:26.770 --> 01:01:26.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1585
01:01:27.870 --> 01:01:32.570
Anyway, something to think about with all our extra time that we have.
总之，趁我们现在有这么多空闲时间，可以考虑一下。

1586
01:01:33.070 --> 01:01:33.730
I know.
我知道。

1587
01:01:33.870 --> 01:01:37.790
I just think about there's so many languages I want to learn that are spoken in countries
我只是在想，还有好多我想学的语言，都是在那些国家通用的语言，

1588
01:01:38.270 --> 01:01:40.190
that, you know, I would like...
就是，你知道，我想……

1589
01:01:40.190 --> 01:01:41.970
You already speak three languages, Angela.
安吉拉，你已经会说三种语言了。

1590
01:01:42.250 --> 01:01:44.810
I do, but why not go back and, like, learn more?
我是会，但为什么不回去再多学点呢？

1591
01:01:45.030 --> 01:01:47.670
Like, be truly proficient in Spanish or something.
比如，真正精通西班牙语之类的。

1592
01:01:47.930 --> 01:01:48.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1593
01:01:48.610 --> 01:01:49.810
I wish I spoke Spanish.
我真希望我会说西班牙语。

1594
01:01:50.290 --> 01:01:51.050
You can.
你可以学的。

1595
01:01:53.030 --> 01:01:55.150
I'm French when I'm angry, and that's it.
我只有在生气的时候才会说法语，也就那样了。

1596
01:01:55.930 --> 01:01:56.250
Oh.
哦。

1597
01:01:56.610 --> 01:01:57.510
Angry French.
生气的法语。

1598
01:01:58.070 --> 01:01:59.010
Where are we?
我们聊到哪了？

1599
01:01:59.110 --> 01:02:00.270
Oh, you know where we should go?
哦，你知道我们该去哪吗？

1600
01:02:00.390 --> 01:02:00.630
Where?
去哪？

1601
01:02:00.630 --> 01:02:02.870
We should go back on the road with Pam and Nellie.
我们应该和帕姆还有奈莉一起回到路上。

1602
01:02:03.170 --> 01:02:03.270
Okay.
好的。

1603
01:02:03.270 --> 01:02:06.490
Because they are bonding about Pam's murals.
因为她们正在聊帕姆的壁画，增进感情。

1604
01:02:07.330 --> 01:02:09.770
Pam painted Angela's nursery?
帕姆画了安吉拉的婴儿房？

1605
01:02:10.030 --> 01:02:11.370
That was a bombshell.
那真是个重磅炸弹。

1606
01:02:11.570 --> 01:02:11.790
I mean...
我是说……

1607
01:02:11.790 --> 01:02:12.590
I was not expecting.
我完全没想到。

1608
01:02:12.590 --> 01:02:13.790
Shut the front door.
简直不敢相信。

1609
01:02:14.050 --> 01:02:14.330
Yeah.
是啊。

1610
01:02:14.330 --> 01:02:19.270
I cannot believe Angela trusted Pam to paint her baby nursery.
我真不敢相信安吉拉竟然信任帕姆，让她去画婴儿房。

1611
01:02:19.570 --> 01:02:21.930
I can't believe Angela let Pam in her home.
我不敢相信安吉拉竟然让帕姆进了她的家门。

1612
01:02:22.090 --> 01:02:22.890
Well, there's that.
嗯，确实如此。

1613
01:02:23.190 --> 01:02:28.710
We learned that she did Angela's nursery, and, you know, I guess there were a bunch of
我们得知她画了安吉拉的婴儿房，而且，你知道，我想里面画了一堆

1614
01:02:28.710 --> 01:02:32.870
animals, but they all had to be fully clothed, like the lion was in a tuxedo.
动物，但它们都必须穿得整整齐齐，比如那头狮子穿着燕尾服。

1615
01:02:32.870 --> 01:02:37.450
Well, you have something in common with Angela Martin, which is that you love pictures of
嗯，你和安吉拉·马丁有一个共同点，那就是你们都喜欢

1616
01:02:37.450 --> 01:02:39.270
animals and little outfits, Ange.
动物穿小衣服的照片，安吉。

1617
01:02:39.390 --> 01:02:39.750
I do.
我确实喜欢。

1618
01:02:39.910 --> 01:02:41.310
Little hats and vests and things.
小帽子、小背心之类的东西。

1619
01:02:41.450 --> 01:02:42.010
You know...
你知道……

1620
01:02:42.010 --> 01:02:44.330
I mean, a cowboy hamster will make your day.
我是说，一只牛仔仓鼠就能让你开心一整天。

1621
01:02:44.450 --> 01:02:44.950
Get out.
别开玩笑了。

1622
01:02:45.210 --> 01:02:46.330
With a little leather veSt.
还穿着一件小皮背心。

1623
01:02:46.330 --> 01:02:50.690
If you could get a little vest on a hamster, I would lose my mind.
如果你能给仓鼠穿上一件小背心，我绝对会疯掉的。

1624
01:02:52.630 --> 01:02:57.910
Nellie is going to get a text while she is driving Pam around, so Pam's like, I'll read
奈莉在开车带帕姆到处转的时候收到了一条短信，所以帕姆说，我帮你读吧。

1625
01:02:57.910 --> 01:02:58.570
it for you.
那是安迪发来的一个新项目。

1626
01:02:58.870 --> 01:03:01.090
And it is a new project from Andy.
他想让她为办公室里的每个人制作一份家谱，而且他特别

1627
01:03:01.270 --> 01:03:05.630
He would like her to make a family tree for everyone in the office, and he's particularly
对那些黑料感兴趣。

1628
01:03:05.630 --> 01:03:07.090
interested in the dirt.
挖掘黑料。

1629
01:03:07.390 --> 01:03:08.310
Dig up dirt.
所以奈莉说，我们得编造一堆谎话。

1630
01:03:09.330 --> 01:03:12.090
So Nellie's like, we have to come up with a bunch of lies.
是啊。

1631
01:03:12.970 --> 01:03:13.410
Yeah.
她就是想捉弄他。

1632
01:03:13.650 --> 01:03:15.170
She wants to just mess with him.
帕姆打算让她说吉姆和理查德·尼克松有亲戚关系。

1633
01:03:15.710 --> 01:03:19.030
Pam is going to tell her to say that Jim is related to Richard Nixon.
她说这是一个内部梗。

1634
01:03:19.030 --> 01:03:20.970
She says it's an inside joke.
是啊。

1635
01:03:21.270 --> 01:03:21.410
Yeah.
他刚睡醒的时候看起来确实很像尼克松。

1636
01:03:21.530 --> 01:03:23.550
He looks very Nixon-y when he wakes up.
就在这时，帕姆透露她确实觉得吉姆有什么事瞒着

1637
01:03:23.730 --> 01:03:27.450
And this is when Pam shares that she does feel like there's something Jim isn't telling
